  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#31970\", \"PowerToys#32935\", \"PowerToys#32279\"], \"answer\": \"A macro recorder for keyboard and mouse input has been requested several times, and this is a feature request that PowerToys does not currently offer. Your request has been folded into the existing ones (#31970 is the main thread; #32935 and #32279 were closed as duplicates of other macro threads), so add a thumbs-up to #31970 and describe your use case there. In the meantime, the maintainers' suggested workaround is Power Automate Desktop, which is built into Windows: record a flow of your repetitive steps and assign a keyboard shortcut to it. It can be edited afterward. Note that one commenter asked whether it needs admin permission, and the thread does not answer that. A related proposal for a hotkey-triggered keyboard Macro utility (#47614) exists, but it has no recorder in v1, only manual step entry.\"}",
